# docs_everywhere C++ bindings

A header-only C++17 wrapper over the `docs_everywhere` C ABI. `docs_everywhere.hpp`
includes the C header beside it; every declaration lives in
`namespace docs_everywhere`.

## Prerequisites

- CMake 3.14 or later
- A C++17 compiler
- The `docs_everywhere` native library (`libdocs_everywhere.so`, `libdocs_everywhere.dylib`, or
  `docs_everywhere.dll`)

## Use with CMake

```cmake
add_subdirectory(path/to/cpp)
add_executable(app main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE docs_everywhere::cpp)
```

`docs_everywhere::cpp` adds this directory to the include path, requires
C++17, and links the native library: the file named by the `DOCS_EVERYWHERE_LIBRARY`
CMake cache variable or environment variable when set, or else
`docs_everywhere` by name.

```cpp
#include "docs_everywhere.hpp"
```

The first free function, constructor, or static member you call checks
that the linked library matches these headers and throws
`docs_everywhere::LoadError` if it doesn't; call `docs_everywhere::check_library()`
at startup to check eagerly.

